.TH mktemp 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
mktemp \- create a temporary file or directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY mktemp
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ TEMPLATE ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Create a temporary file or directory, safely, and print its name.
TEMPLATE must contain at least 3 consecutive 'X's in last component.
If TEMPLATE is not specified, use tmp.XXXXXXXXXX, and \fB\-\-tmpdir\fR is implied.
Files are created u+rw, and directories u+rwx, minus umask restrictions.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mktemp\-d
\fB\-d, \-\-directory\fP
.UE
create a directory, not a file
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mktemp\-u
\fB\-u, \-\-dry\-run\fP
.UE
do not create anything; merely print a name (unsafe)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mktemp\-q
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fP
.UE
suppress diagnostics about file/dir\-creation failure
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mktemp\-\-suffix
\fB\-\-suffix=SUFF\fP
.UE
append SUFF to TEMPLATE; SUFF must not contain a slash.
This option is implied if TEMPLATE does not end in X
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mktemp\-p
\fB\-p DIR, \-\-tmpdir[=\,DIR]\fP
.UE
interpret TEMPLATE relative to DIR;
if DIR is not specified, use $TMPDIR if set, else \fI\,/tmp\/\fP.
With this option, TEMPLATE must not be an absolute name;
unlike with \fB\-t\fR, TEMPLATE may contain slashes,
but mktemp creates only the final component
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#mktemp\-t
\fB\-t\fP
.UE
interpret TEMPLATE as a single file name component,
relative to a directory: $TMPDIR, if set;
else the directory specified via \fB\-p\fR; else \fI\,/tmp\/\fP [deprecated]
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/mktemp#mktemp\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/mktemp#mktemp\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
